{
  "_file": "qos_bindings_vectors.json",
  "_brief": "The 11 S2.4.7 qos document, plus the QoS every golden key must resolve to",
  "_source": [
    "qos.profiles / qos.bindings / qos.rt_override below are transcribed from the",
    "json5 block in 11 S2.4.7 (grep 'key 前缀 -> 档位'). Field order and the order",
    "of the bindings array are preserved verbatim: 11 S2.4.7 makes 首个匹配生效 the",
    "resolution rule, so the ARRAY ORDER IS THE SEMANTICS and reordering this file",
    "changes what the emergency-stop keys resolve to.",
    "The vectors are derived by hand from that array plus the frozen profile table",
    "in 11 S2.4.2, and each one records which binding index and match expression it",
    "expects to win -- an expectation on the resulting knobs alone would pass for",
    "any other binding that happens to name the same profile.",
    "This file is a TEST FIXTURE and not deployment configuration. configs/",
    "common.yaml declares qos.profiles and qos.bindings as null key positions, so",
    "the stack refuses to start until a deployment supplies them; populating",
    "configs/ is a separate item and must not be done from here."
  ],
  "_depth_sentinel": [
    "handler.depth 0 inside qos.profiles is 11 S2.4.7's spelling for 'no default,",
    "deployment must supply it, otherwise refuse to start'. In the vectors below",
    "that same state is written as null, which is the configs/ convention for an",
    "unassigned value. Q4_stream is the profile in that state today.",
    "11 S2.4.2 does now compute N = 10 for Q4 from a 200 ms jitter buffer over",
    "20 ms chunks, and it is deliberately NOT written here: the same paragraph",
    "keeps the value pending QoS-T8, and a number placed in a fixture cannot be",
    "told apart later from a number that was calibrated."
  ],
  "robot_id": "dog-01",
  "qos": {
    "profiles": {
      "Q0_safety": {"congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true, "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}},
      "Q1_rt": {"congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true, "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}},
      "Q2_state": {"congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "data_high", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false, "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}},
      "Q3_cmd": {"congestion_control": "block", "priority": "data", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false, "handler": {"kind": "fifo", "depth": 256}},
      "Q4_stream": {"congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "interactive_high", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": false, "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 0}}
    },
    "bindings": [
      {"match": "xbrain/*/cmd/estop", "profile": "Q0_safety"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/cmd/estop/ack", "profile": "Q0_safety"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/safety/**", "profile": "Q0_safety"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/probe/estop/**", "profile": "Q0_safety"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/cmd/chassis/ctrl", "profile": "Q0_safety"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/cmd/chassis/ctrl/ack", "profile": "Q0_safety"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/audio/mic", "profile": "Q1_rt", "set": {"handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}}},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/audio/play", "profile": "Q1_rt", "set": {"handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}}},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/teleop/input", "profile": "Q1_rt"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/lidar/points", "profile": "Q1_rt", "set": {"priority": "interactive_high"}},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/lidar/grid", "profile": "Q1_rt", "set": {"priority": "interactive_high"}},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/perception/**", "profile": "Q1_rt"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/gnss/**", "profile": "Q1_rt"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/lidar/**", "profile": "Q1_rt"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/**/cmd_vel", "profile": "Q1_rt"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/**/status", "profile": "Q2_state"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/**/state", "profile": "Q2_state"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/chassis/**", "profile": "Q2_state"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/rt/**", "profile": "Q3_cmd"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/cmd/teleop", "profile": "Q1_rt", "set": {"handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}}},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/state/targets", "profile": "Q2_state", "set": {"priority": "data"}},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/state/**", "profile": "Q2_state"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/health/summary", "profile": "Q2_state"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/audio/**", "profile": "Q4_stream"},
      {"match": "xbrain/*/**", "profile": "Q3_cmd"}
    ],
    "rt_override": {"congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "interactive_high", "handler": {"kind": "fifo", "depth": 32}}
  },
  "vectors": [
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/cmd/estop",
      "why": "S2.4.5 第 7 条: estop is single-listed as Q0 so that Q3's block can never turn a pressed button into a 3 s wait",
      "binding_index": 0, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/cmd/estop", "profile": "Q0_safety",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/cmd/estop/ack",
      "why": "the ack terminates the 10 Hz resend window in S2.4.5 第 7 条, so it needs the same queue as the command",
      "binding_index": 1, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/cmd/estop/ack", "profile": "Q0_safety",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/cmd/chassis/ctrl",
      "why": "S2.4.7 v0.3 added it as Q0 because S9.3.3 makes it the only path out of hes_lock and timeout_lock",
      "binding_index": 4, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/cmd/chassis/ctrl", "profile": "Q0_safety",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/cmd/chassis/ctrl/ack",
      "why": "same unlock path as its command; a lower queue here would leave the unlock unconfirmed",
      "binding_index": 5, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/cmd/chassis/ctrl/ack", "profile": "Q0_safety",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/safety/estop",
      "why": "the v0.3 repair itself: before it, this key fell through to rt/** and lost real_time plus express, which S2.2.12 calls the most serious row it found",
      "binding_index": 2, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/safety/**", "profile": "Q0_safety",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/probe/estop/ping",
      "why": "the other half of the v0.3 repair: the old probe/estop rule matched no sub-segment, so ping and pong landed in the xbrain/*/** fallback and acquired block",
      "binding_index": 3, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/probe/estop/**", "profile": "Q0_safety",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "reliable", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 8}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/audio/mic",
      "why": "S2.2.12 QoS gap table: 50 Hz audio on FIFO grows lag without bound, so the binding sets Ring(4) over Q1",
      "binding_index": 6, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/audio/mic", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/audio/play",
      "why": "same argument as the mic direction",
      "binding_index": 7, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/audio/play", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/teleop/input",
      "why": "Ring(1) from Q1 unchanged; S2.2.12 notes FIFO here made the S12A.9.6 age check vacuous",
      "binding_index": 8, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/teleop/input", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/lidar/points",
      "why": "S2.4.2 档内例外: 175 KB frames drop to interactive_high so they stop sharing a queue with cmd_vel and gnss",
      "binding_index": 9, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/lidar/points", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "interactive_high", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/lidar/grid",
      "why": "same exception; Ring(1) is what keeps the RNS grid age check in S2.4.6 meaningful",
      "binding_index": 10, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/lidar/grid", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "interactive_high", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/motion/cmd_vel",
      "why": "reached through rt/**/cmd_vel, not through any domain-specific rule; block here is what S2.4.5 第 1 条 traces to Tier 1 locking the machine",
      "binding_index": 14, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/**/cmd_vel", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/chassis/state",
      "why": "the non-obvious one: rt/**/state wins over rt/chassis/** because it is written first, and S2.4.7 keeps that rule as the catch-all stopping any RT state key from landing in Q3-rt",
      "binding_index": 16, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/**/state", "profile": "Q2_state",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "data_high", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/rt/behavior/request",
      "why": "the other non-obvious one: no specific rule covers it, so it falls to rt/** and Q3_cmd, and QOS-C1 then rewrites it to Q3-rt because block on the RT plane has no upper bound",
      "binding_index": 18, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/rt/**", "profile": "Q3_cmd",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "interactive_high", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false,
      "handler": {"kind": "fifo", "depth": 32}, "rt_override_applied": true
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/cmd/teleop",
      "why": "S2.2.12 gap table: Q3's block here would stall the p5_gateway receive thread and take the whole cmd/** downlink with it",
      "binding_index": 19, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/cmd/teleop", "profile": "Q1_rt",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "real_time", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": true,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 1}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/state/targets",
      "why": "S2.4.2 档内例外: the mask-carrying frame is far larger than other state keys, so it drops to data rather than crowding the state queue",
      "binding_index": 20, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/state/targets", "profile": "Q2_state",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "data", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/health/summary",
      "why": "its own rule rather than the fallback, because health/summary is periodic state and the fallback is block plus FIFO(256)",
      "binding_index": 22, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/health/summary", "profile": "Q2_state",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "data_high", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": 4}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/health/bit",
      "why": "the fallback, and correctly so: S2.4.2 lists health/bit under Q3 with cmd/**, event/** and data/**",
      "binding_index": 24, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/**", "profile": "Q3_cmd",
      "congestion_control": "block", "priority": "data", "reliability": "reliable", "express": false,
      "handler": {"kind": "fifo", "depth": 256}, "rt_override_applied": false
    },
    {
      "key": "xbrain/dog-01/audio/broadcast",
      "why": "Q4, and its depth is the one the deployment still owes: S2.4.7 writes 0, S13.15 lists that exact condition under E_QOS_VIOLATION, so require_handler_depth() must refuse rather than pick a number",
      "binding_index": 23, "binding_match": "xbrain/*/audio/**", "profile": "Q4_stream",
      "congestion_control": "drop", "priority": "interactive_high", "reliability": "best_effort", "express": false,
      "handler": {"kind": "ring", "depth": null}, "rt_override_applied": false
    }
  ]
}
